Description: Wild OS changes to Plasma and KWin
 Patched copies of a few Plasma and KWin files, where the Wild OS design
 cannot be reached by configuration:
 .
  * the panel view, so one panel draws the taskbar as the design's two
    separate glass pills, around Start and the apps and around the status
    area, with pop-ups 14 px above them as drawn;
  * the Aurorae title bar, so window titles read "Documents - Files" with a
    hyphen as on Windows;
  * the right-click menu of the taskbar's empty space (Task Manager,
    taskbar settings, show the desktop) in place of Plasma's widget menu;
  * a KWin plugin that draws the window menu (title bar right click and
    Alt+Space) with the Wild OS menu in place of KWin's own;
  * a KWin effect that rounds the bottom corners of decorated windows to
    the title bar's 14 px radius, with the edge and shadow carried round,
    and squares the corners of maximised, full screen and snapped windows;
  * two KWin effects for Settings > Accessibility, off until turned on
    there: an outline round every window with a thick accent ring round
    the one in use, and a blur that softens and dims every window but the
    one in use;
  * a KWin script that draws the taskbar underglow chosen in Settings, a
    glowing line along the top edge of the docked taskbar;
  * a "Wild OS" sign-in session in place of Plasma's own entries.
 .
 The patched files are taken from the Plasma and KWin versions named in the
 dependencies; an upgrade past them needs the patches rebased first.
